<section class="blk">
  <h2 id="s-rosario-colla">Rosario-Colla &mdash; not a gap, an origin</h2>
  <div class="prose">
    <p>Colonia was carried here for days as the one Uruguayan department still unaccounted for.
    <strong>It was never unaccounted for &mdash; it is where they came from.</strong> The marriage of
    3 February 1837 at San José de Mayo gives Mauricio Lerena's birthplace as <strong>Colla</strong>,
    the old name of <strong>Rosario, Colonia</strong>, and names his parents.</p>
    <p>What was genuinely missing is that <strong>none of them were people here</strong>. Mauricio is
    the man on whom the whole finding rests &mdash; his children account for San José, Flores and
    Florida, with Salto and Montevideo besides &mdash; and he was
    <strong>the patriarch this archive had researched but never made a person</strong>, living here
    only inside other people's notes until 20 September 2026.</p>
  </div>
