<section class="blk">
  <h2 id="s-seven-spellings">All seven spellings, put to one collection</h2>
  <div class="prose">
    <p>This archive keeps <strong>seven spellings</strong> of the surname. All seven have now been put
    to <em>Uruguay, Census Records, 1726&ndash;1858</em>. <strong>Serena alone returned two complete
    households</strong>, and <strong>Sancho is not among the Lerena results at all</strong> &mdash; he
    is indexed Llerena. That is the whole argument for sweeping spellings rather than searching a name.</p>
    <p>Three of the seven returned nothing, and they are tested nulls rather than silences: Serena
    returns ten and Llerena three on the identical query, so the form works.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="scroll" style="margin-top:18px">
